      "text": "To compute \\(\\cos 150^\\circ\\), we can use the angle subtraction formula for cosine. The angle \\(150^\\circ\\) can be expressed as \\(180^\\circ - 30^\\circ\\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\cos 150^\\circ = \\cos (180^\\circ - 30^\\circ)\n\\]\nUsing the cosine subtraction formula \\(\\cos (180^\\circ - \\theta) = -\\cos \\theta\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\cos 150^\\circ = -\\cos 30^\\circ\n\\]\nWe know that \\(\\cos 30^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\). Substituting this value in, we get:\n\\[\n\\cos 150^\\circ = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n\\]\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}\n\\]",
